[%emt 0:01:55] [%think 10936] [%out 11228] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0]
[%cachewrite 1379] Black's bishop just captured my knight on f5. The only way
to win the material back is e4xf5 with the pawn: - The bishop on f3 cannot
reach f5, and my own f4 pawn blocks the rook on f1. - An in-between move such
as e5 does not work. After dxe5 fxe5 Qxe5, Black keeps the extra piece. After
exf5, material is level. My f5 pawn also attacks the knight on g6. That knight
has almost nowhere safe to go: - Ne5 loses to fxe5. - Nxf4 loses the knight to
Bxf4. - Nh4 puts it on the rim, where I can later try to trap it with g3. Next
move I need to watch for ...Qb6. It pins my e3 bishop against the king along
the b6–g1 diagonal. I can answer it with Qd4 or c5. } 13... Nh4 14. Qd3 {
